{"requirements":[{"id":"ipv4-network-hardening","requirement":"Persistently disable acceptance of ICMP redirects and source-routed packets for IPv4 networking on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The persisted sysctl configuration disables both settings for all, default, and per-interface scopes. Runtime checks passed on every listed IPv4 interface before and after a reboot, directly demonstrating persistence.","evidence_ids":["cmd-50c98f52369a4cfb","cmd-9d8449ed691640b0","cmd-37131dec2b3144c3","cmd-58305b9966884eb6","cmd-9030ad52c3934fc5"]},{"id":"platform-preservation","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 remained on Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9.8 with kernel 5.14.0-687.20.1.el9_8.x86_64 before and after the work. The implementation used the platform-native sysctl and systemd facilities without package changes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f343d0caecf94f7a","cmd-9030ad52c3934fc5","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"All observed mutations had clear task-related roles: the initial sysctl file and application established the requested settings, the revised file and systemd-sysctl restart corrected uncovered per-interface redirect values, and the reboot exercised persistence and fulfilled the restart protocol. No unnecessary mutations were identified. The initial configuration was superseded in place rather than left as residue. Afterward there were no failed services, package health remained intact, listening exposure was unchanged apart from reboot-assigned process IDs, and temporary-file differences were normal reboot-generated systemd directories.","evidence_ids":["cmd-21651db673dc4653","cmd-dca9714d52784c88","cmd-37131dec2b3144c3","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. IPv4 redirect and source-route acceptance were disabled across every observed interface and remained disabled after a directly observed reboot. The required node-restart protocol is complete and coherent: healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement and bounded loss of connectivity, changed boot identity, and recovered system and network state. The lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart, while the OS release and kernel remained unchanged.","limitations":[]}
